    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 tests pass \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` fields are now unified into a single **`memberId`** formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (e.g. the test run produced `NSW2716E6609E1` = `NSW` + `27` + `16E6609E` + Luhn digit `1`), and the standalone `checkDigit` field is gone.\n\n**Identity assembly** (`OwnerRestControllerV1`)\n- Replaced `assignCustomerCode` + `assignMembershipNumber` with a single `assignMemberId`: `region + FY2 + HASH8`, then a Luhn `CHK` over that body's digits, then collision-dedup.\n- Collision handling (`deduplicateMemberId`) now applies to `memberId`, comparing against existing `getMemberId()`.\n- The `CHK` is computed over `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` *before* any `-<n>` collision suffix, per spec.\n\n**Owner segment / locality** \u2014 `OwnerLocality.fromCustomerCode` \u2192 `fromMemberId`, now reading the region as a prefix match (`NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`, else `UNKNOWN`) since the memberId has no `-` delimiter. `locality`, `timezone`, and `ownerSegment` all derive from `memberId`.\n\n**Audit record** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent`'s component renamed `customerCode` \u2192 `memberId` (JSON is now `{seq,ownerId,memberId,membershipLevel,event}`); the human-readable audit line and `primaryIdentifier` both reference `memberId`.\n\n**Supporting changes**\n- `Owner` entity: `customer_code`/`membership_number` columns \u2192 single `member_id`.\n- `OwnerMapper`: dropped the `checkDigit` mapping, retargeted locality/timezone/ownerSegment expressions, `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `memberId`.\n- Renamed `CustomerCodeCheckDigit` \u2192 `MemberIdCheckDigit` (Luhn helper, still used for `CHK`).\n- `openapi.yml`: removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` schemas; added `memberId`; updated `locality` description.\n- All four DB `schema.sql` files (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres): `customer_code` + `membership_number` \u2192 `member_id`.\n\nThe `fiscalYear` DTO field is unchanged (still derived from `registrationDate`); its value now also lives inside `memberId` as the `FY` segment.",
